From: Nguyen Phan <nguyen@nguyenphan.org>
Date: Mon, 10 Nov 2026 20:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] lane_host: read a request's slot under the lock

submitFn read the request's slot — freeSlot walks the admitted and queued lists — before taking the
mutex, while every other reader and writer holds it. A concurrent append's reallocation could free
the buffer under the walk: the segfault at lane_host.zig:433 on 2026-11-03, 11-04, 11-06, 11-07
(twice) and 11-09, each one a whole-engine restart. The read moves under the lock.
---

diff --git a/zig/src/core/lane_host.zig b/zig/src/core/lane_host.zig
index 0f944ec4..d7566b81 100644
--- a/zig/src/core/lane_host.zig
+++ b/zig/src/core/lane_host.zig
@@ -396,9 +396,13 @@ pub const LaneHost = struct {
     fn submitFn(ctx: *anyopaque, id: Id, request: *const Request, sink: Sink) SubmitError!void {
         const h = self(ctx);
         const job = h.gpa.create(Job) catch return error.Busy;
-        job.* = .{ .host = h, .id = id, .request = request, .sink = sink, .slot = h.freeSlot() };
         h.mutex.lockUncancelable(h.io);
         defer h.mutex.unlock(h.io);
+        // The slot is read from the admitted and queued lists: under the lock, like every other reader and
+        // writer of them. Unlocked, a concurrent append's reallocation frees the buffer while freeSlot walks
+        // it — the segfault at lane_host.zig:433 seen on the pair 2026-11-03, 11-04, 11-06, 11-07 (twice) and
+        // 11-09, each one a whole-engine restart.
+        job.* = .{ .host = h, .id = id, .request = request, .sink = sink, .slot = h.freeSlot() };
         if (h.closing or h.isBroken()) { // (a broken pair admits nothing more: the process restarts)
             h.gpa.destroy(job);
             return error.Closed;
